219 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 129 0 R
/E (MakeCode Arcade is an educational platform developed by Microsoft, designed to introduce students and educators to programming through the creation of video games. Accessible online, it offers a rich and intuitive environment where users can design, customize, and share their own games. MakeCode Arcade's interface is suitable for all levels of programming experience, offering both a so-called "block-based" mode for beginners and a text-based mode for more advanced users.)
/Pg 9 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
220 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 129 0 R
/E (MakeCode Arcade is not just about creating video games: it offers a free and creative space where students can tell stories, create animations, and bring their ideas to life. This flexibility allows them to fully express themselves, test innovative concepts, and develop interactive narratives that reflect their imaginations and interests.)
/Pg 9 0 R
/K [5 6]
>>
endobj
221 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 800 0 R
/E (Committed to inclusive and innovative pedagogy, MakeCode Arcade empowers students to experiment, learn, and grow while positively contributing to their community. Using a Skill Map approach, the platform offers a personalized and progressive learning path, incorporating gamification elements such as unlockable achievements and visual progress indicators. These tools motivate users to explore, acquire specific skills, and visualize their progress in a fun way.)
/Pg 9 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
