438 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 140 0 R
/E (Skill maps are visual guides that show the steps to achieving a goal, such as creating a game in MakeCode Arcade. They break down skills into small levels, allowing you to track your progress, see what you've learned, and what you still need to learn. These cards are easy to follow and allow students to learn at their own pace. As they progress through the Skill Maps, they discover programming basics like loops, variables, and conditions, while having fun creating games. Skill Maps aren't just about coding: they also include design, storytelling, and rule-making skills, so everyone can develop their own ideas. They are designed to be engaging and tailored to each student's interests, making learning fun and accessible to all.)
/Pg 20 0 R
/K [9]
>>
